  "body": "Two tests in `crates/app/tests/wire_post.rs` posted to fixed paths `rough-only` and `right-only` in the system temp folder. On the shared runner, another user owns those files. The write failed with \"Permission denied (os error 13)\".\n\nWhat changed:\n- Both posts now write into a `tempfile::tempdir()` folder, kept alive for the scope of the test. Line 337 of the same file already does this.\n- Nothing else changed.\n\nSearch of `crates/*/tests` for other fixed `temp_dir().join(\"<literal>\")` names:\n- `crates/app/tests/machine_edit.rs:251` uses a fixed folder name `camcraft_temp_names`. Not changed: it is outside this issue.\n- `crates/motion/tests/headless_bin.rs:36` uses a path that must not exist. Correct as is.\n- `crates/ui/tests/catalog_render.rs:134` is a fallback for an output folder. Not a test write target.\n\nPinning tests (both pass on head e24f6bacf, log `gate-4400-e24f6bacf.log`):\n- `a_centre_slit_with_a_skim_generates_verifies_and_posts`\n- `an_open_run_with_a_skim_generates_verifies_and_posts`\n\nAlso run: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`. Both green.\n\nNot exercised: a red-before run. A path owned by another user cannot be made here. The light lane did not run: no code under test changed.\n\nThis PR does not fix the `rough_finish` catalog timeouts or the runner clippy fault that #4400 also tracks.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: low\n\nRefs #4400\n",
